{
  "_id": "tg-worship",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "I and the lad will go yonder and worship, Gen. 22:5. Thou shalt have no other gods before me, Ex. 20:3 (32:1–8, 19–35; 34:14; Deut. 6:13–14). Come up … and seventy of the elders … and worship ye afar off, Ex. 24:1. shouldest be driven to worship them, Deut. 4:19. serve the Lord thy God with all thy heart, Deut. 10:12. hath gone and served other gods, and worshipped them, Deut. 17:3. worship the Lord in the beauty of holiness, 1 Chr. 16:29 (Ps. 29:2; 96:9). in thy fear will I worship, Ps. 5:7. kindreds of the nations shall worship before thee, Ps. 22:27. earth shall worship thee, Ps. 66:4. neither shalt thou worship any strange god, Ps. 81:9. All nations … shall come and worship before thee, Ps. 86:9 (Rev. 15:4). let us worship and bow down, Ps. 95:6. Exalt ye the Lord … and worship at his footstool, Ps. 99:5 (132:7). calf in Horeb, and worshipped the molten image, Ps. 106:19. I will worship toward thy holy temple, Ps. 138:2. they worship the work of their own hands, Isa. 2:8 (2 Ne. 12:8). worship the Lord in the holy mount at Jerusalem, Isa. 27:13. this people … have removed their heart far from me, Isa. 29:13 (2 Ne. 27:25). he maketh a god, and worshippeth it, Isa. 44:15. they fall down, yea, they worship, Isa. 46:6. shall all flesh come to worship before me, Isa. 66:23. sun … whom they have worshipped, Jer. 8:2. no more worship the work of thine hands, Micah 5:13 (3 Ne. 21:17). men shall worship him, every one from his place, Zeph. 2:11. unto Jerusalem to worship the King, Zech. 14:17.",
